# The IOMMU (QEMU's SMMUv3), which the tests' machines have: Veda's kernel
# passes the DMA of Veda's own devices through, while the driver VM's reach
# only its memory, and the ITS keeps each device to its own interrupts. Both
# work at once, without a fault: the disks, Veda's; the sound card (HD
# Audio), the USB controller with its keyboard and tablet, and the network
# card, Linux's.
sound hda
input usb
net ethernet
nettest local
fail-on "PANIC"
fail-on "nettest: FAIL"
wait-serial "iommu: SMMUv3 at" 60
wait-serial "desktop ready" 600
wait-serial "input: QEMU QEMU USB Keyboard (usb 0627:0001): keyboard" 300
wait-serial "alsa: attached to the audio service" 300
wait-serial "nettest: PASS" 600
reject-serial "iommu: unit at"
reject-serial "iommu: not used"
